A vast river delta viewed from above in the style of Leonardo da Vinci's detailed anatomical sketches, rendered in sepia ink on aged parchment. The river splits into dozens of branching channels, some flowing smoothly while others twist into complex loops and eddies. Small paper boats and folded documents drift along the various streams, some getting caught in whirlpools, others gliding effortlessly toward a distant horizon. The channels are bordered by intricate mechanical gears and cogs partially submerged in the water, suggesting an underlying engine directing the flow. Cross-hatching technique creates depth and shadow, with careful annotations and measurement lines scattered throughout like architectural studies, though containing no readable text—only abstract marks and symbols.
